// `src/syntax/syntax.npk` — THE PATTERN PARSER'S LAYER ENTRY. A module above
// `syntax` writes one import, this file, and reaches what the layer offers.
//
// FILLED BY cycle 0.1, governed by `meta/specs/SYNTAX.md`. Pattern text to an
// AST, driven by an EXPLICIT STACK and never by native recursion (RX-032,
// `SAFETY.md` S-18) so that a deeply nested pattern is a refusal and not a
// blown call stack. `tests/probe/probe05_explicit_stack.npk` is the evidence
// that the shape is both writable and sufficient: 10 000 levels deep is
// refused at depth 251 and the program survives.
//
// SINCE CYCLE 0.1.0 THE LAYER HOLDS THE PIECES EVERY LATER SUBCYCLE IS WRITTEN
// IN: `pattern_error.npk` (the closed kind list and the one constructor, RX-172),
// `cursor.npk` (the byte cursor, RX-173), `ast.npk` (the arena, RX-174) and
// `parse.npk` (the parser's entry and its first refusal, RX-175).
// `tests/unit/syntax_skeleton.npk` shows they compose, through this file's
// re-exports alone. SINCE CYCLE 0.1.1 `parse.npk` PARSES THE CORE GRAMMAR --
// `parse_pattern`, RX-182 … RX-186 -- and classes, escapes other than
// punctuation, and flags are the subcycles' after it (Y-31).
// SINCE CYCLE 0.1.2 ITS STACK IS BOUNDED: a `(` that would nest groups deeper than
// `NREGEX_NEST_DEPTH` is `NestTooDeep` at that `(` (Y-35, RX-193).
// SINCE CYCLE 0.1.3 IT PARSES CLASSES -- members, ranges, nested classes, the
// operators, Perl classes, properties and POSIX classes inside a class, unresolved
// (Y-36 … Y-38, RX-197) -- groups and classes nesting at most `NREGEX_NEST_DEPTH` deep
// together (RX-198).
// SINCE CYCLE 0.1.4 IT READS ESCAPES AND FLAGS -- every escape of §1, in a class and out,
// and `(?flags)` and `(?flags:...)`, with `x` and `(?-u)` (Y-40 … Y-43, RX-203 … RX-208).
//
// EVERY LINE BELOW IS `pub use`, ONE NAME PER LINE (`BUILD.md` B-15a rules 1
// and 3): `use` is not transitive, a plain `use` re-exports nothing, and one
// name to a line keeps the list greppable and a removal one line of diff. Each
// section names the decision that put it here.
//
// LAYERING (`BUILD.md` §6, rule B-16). May import: `unicode`, `core`. A program
// importing this file owes `core`'s eleven arms (measured at `c970483`), because
// `pattern_error.npk` imports `core`.
mod:syntax;

